<title>SWEDEN: Perstorp sells Lumac to Celsis.</title>
<headline>Perstorp sells Lumac to Celsis.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish chemicals company Perstorp AB said on Monday it would sell microbiology firm Lumac BV in Holland to Britain's Celsis International Plc as part of a restructuring plan.</p>
<p>The purchase price was 11.2 million pounds, Perstorp said in a statement.</p>
<p>Lumac BV in Holland, whose British subsidiary Lumac Ltd is also included in the deal, has an annual turnover of 55 million crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;The spin off, which takes effect on August 31, 1996 will have a positive effect on Perstorp's result for the 1995/96 financial year, but this fits within the group's forecast of a result of around 700 million crowns,&quot; Perstorp said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
